      "lineAnnotations": {
        "0": {"synopsis":"The 128K starts here (and on a reset): interrupts off, a delay of $692B rounds, then\nRAM_TEST."},
        "1": {"comment":"$692B rounds"},
        "4": {"synopsis":"The delay."},
        "9": {"comment":"To the RAM test"},
        "16": {"synopsis":"RST $10: ROM 1's RST $10 (CALL_ROM1), which prints A through the current channel."},
        "24": {"synopsis":"RST $18: ROM 1's RST $18 (CALL_ROM1): the character at CH_ADD."},
        "32": {"synopsis":"RST $20: ROM 1's RST $20 (CALL_ROM1): the next character at CH_ADD."},
        "40": {"synopsis":"RST $28: calls the routine in ROM 1 whose address is the word after the RST, then returns\npast the word:\n1. HL = that address; $5B5A = the place after the word, the return point.\n2. CALL_ROM1_GO stacks the RAM routine at $5B14 (ROM1_RETURN's copy) as the routine's\n   return, then the address, and jumps to $5B00 (SWAP_ROM's copy), whose RET enters ROM 1\n   there with HL as it was.\n3. When the routine returns, $5B14 swaps back to this ROM and returns to $5B5A.\nKeeps every register for the routine.","comment":"HL = the place of the word; HL kept on the stack"},
        "42": {"comment":"The word's low byte"},
        "45": {"comment":"$5B5A = past the word: the return point"},
        "49": {"comment":"HL = the word"},
        "52": {"comment":"Into ROM 1"},
        "56": {"synopsis":"INT (interrupt mode 1): runs ROM 1's interrupt routine at $0038: the stack gets INT_RETURN,\n$5B00 (SWAP_ROM's copy, to come back) and $0038, then $5B00 swaps the ROMs and returns into\nROM 1's $0038. Keeps HL."},
        "57": {"comment":"Back here at the end"},
        "61": {"comment":"Back to this ROM before that"},
        "65": {"comment":"ROM 1's interrupt routine"},
        "69": {"comment":"Swap the ROMs and go"},
        "72": {"synopsis":"HL back, and return from the interrupt."},
        "74": {"synopsis":"Paging back to RAM bank 0, ROM 0 and the normal screen ($5B5C = 0), ERR_NR = $FF, then on at\n$0321. Vector $010C."},
        "77": {"comment":"Paging byte 0"},
        "81": {"comment":"$5B5C, the paging byte, kept in step"},
        "85": {"comment":"ERR_NR = $FF: no error"},
        "92": {"synopsis":"CALL_ROM1's second half: the stack gets ROM1_RETURN's copy ($5B14) and the routine's address\n(from $5B58), HL as it was, then SWAP_ROM's copy at $5B00.","comment":"$5B58 = the routine"},
        "95": {"comment":"$5B14 under the caller's HL"},
        "100": {"comment":"The routine's address on top, HL back"},
        "104": {"comment":"Swap the ROMs and go"},
        "107": {"synopsis":"Copied to $5B00 at start-up and run from there (88 bytes, to $00C2): flips the ROM (bit 4 of\nthe paging byte at $5B5C, written to port $7FFD with interrupts off) and returns; a RET made\nwith an address on the stack thus continues in the other ROM. Keeps every register."},
        "112": {"comment":"The paging byte"},
        "115": {"comment":"The other ROM"},
        "121": {"comment":"Port $7FFD"},
        "127": {"synopsis":"At $5B14: where a ROM 1 routine called by CALL_ROM1 returns to: the ROMs swapped back, then\na return to $5B5A, past the RST's word.","comment":"Back to this ROM ($5B00)"},
        "131": {"comment":"The return point under HL"},
        "136": {"synopsis":"At $5B1D: where ROM 1's error handling returns to (start-up and the editor put $5B1D under\nERR_SP): ROM 0 paged in, then the handler at the address in $5B8B (GO_HANDLER)."},
        "140": {"comment":"Bit 4 clear: ROM 0"},
        "154": {"synopsis":"At $5B2F: channel P's input routine (CHANS_128_INIT): ROM 0's $06D8 through CALL_ROM0."},
        "159": {"synopsis":"At $5B34: channel P's output routine: ROM 0's $07CA through CALL_ROM0."},
        "162": {"synopsis":"At $5B37: runs the routine at HL in ROM 0 for a caller in ROM 1: the paging byte kept on the\nstack, ROM 0 paged in with interrupts off, then on at $05E6 in ROM 0; CALL_ROM0_BACK\nrestores the paging. A is passed through the alternate AF."},
        "169": {"comment":"The paging byte kept"},
        "170": {"comment":"ROM 0"},
        "181": {"synopsis":"At $5B4A: the paging byte back from the stack and written, interrupts on; return with A from\nthe alternate AF."},
        "195": {"synopsis":"Jumps to the address in $5B8B: the editor's current handler (start-up and the main loop set\nit)."},
        "199": {"synopsis":"Tests the eight RAM banks, 7 down to 0: each paged in at $C000 (port $7FFD), each byte\nwritten $FF and $00 and read back, then the bank cleared. A failure stops at RAM_FAULT."},
        "201": {"synopsis":"One bank."},
        "204": {"comment":"Bank B - 1 at $C000"},
        "218": {"comment":"$FF written and read back"},
        "224": {"comment":"$00 likewise"},
        "229": {"comment":"The rest cleared"},
        "232": {"comment":"The next bank down"},
        "234": {"comment":"$5B88 = 0"},
        "237": {"comment":"The AY chip: C = $FD, D = $FF (register port $FFFD), E = $BF (data port $BFFD)"},
        "244": {"comment":"Register 14, the I/O port"},
        "249": {"comment":"= $FF"},
        "256": {"synopsis":"Jumps into this ROM at fixed addresses for code elsewhere: ROM 1's hooks use $010F, $0112\nand $0115 (HOOK_REPORT, HOOK_STMT_JUMP, HOOK_STMT_NEXT in sp128-1.rom.dis), and $010C is\nRESET_TO_128; the others go to $17AF, $1838, $1ECF, $1F04, $03A2, $182A, $18A8, $012D,\n$0A05, $11A3, $06D8, $07CA, $08A3 and $08F0."},
        "301": {"synopsis":"Vector $0118: ROM 1's $3B01 (CALL_ROM1)."},
        "305": {"synopsis":"A bank failed the RAM test: the border shows its number (B - 1 in the bank counter) and the\nmachine stops there."},
        "307": {"comment":"Border = the bank"},
        "309": {"synopsis":"Forever."},
        "311": {"synopsis":"After the RAM test:\n1. AY register 7 = $FF; SWAP_ROM and the routines after it copied to $5B00-$5B57; $5B5D =\n   $CF; the stack at $5BFF.\n2. Bank 7 (SELECT_BANK 4): $5B83 = $EBEC, with three bytes there set; $5B85 = $2BEC, $5B87 =\n   1; then bank 0 (SELECT_BANK 5).\n3. As a 48K start: P_RAMT = $FFFF, the UDGs copied below it from ROM 1's letters A-U ($3EAF\n   down, ROM 1's $1661), UDG, RASP/PIP, RAMTOP, CHARS = $3C00, the stack below RAMTOP, IM 1,\n   IY = $5C3A; FLAGS bit 4 set (128 BASIC); interrupts on.\n4. The 128K's own variables: $5B5F = $000B, $5B61, $5B63, $5B65 = 0, $FF24 = $EC00, $5B64 =\n   $50, $5B94 and $5B96 = 10.\n5. CHANS from CHANS_128_INIT, the program, variable and edit-line pointers as in the 48K,\n   the colours ($38), border 7, REPDEL 35 and REPPER 5, KSTATE free, STRMS from STRMS_INIT,\n   ERR_NR = $FF, DF_SZ = 2.\n6. CLS (ROM 1's CLS_CMD), ROM 1's test picture when BREAK is held ($3C04, TEST_SCREEN),\n   COPYRIGHT_MSG printed, then bank 7 and its stack (BANK7_STACK), EDITOR_RESET, and the\n   main menu (MAIN_MENU)."},
        "317": {"comment":"AY register 7 = $FF"},
        "321": {"comment":"The RAM routines to $5B00"},
        "332": {"comment":"$5B5D = $CF"},
        "337": {"comment":"The stack in the 128K's variables page"},
        "340": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "345": {"comment":"IX = $EBEC: $5B83"},
        "365": {"comment":"$5B85 = $2BEC, $5B87 = 1"},
        "376": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "381": {"comment":"P_RAMT = $FFFF"},
        "387": {"comment":"The UDGs: $A8 bytes from $3EAF down (ROM 1's LDDR at $1661)"},
        "398": {"comment":"UDG = the first"},
        "403": {"comment":"RASP/PIP = $40, 0"},
        "410": {"comment":"RAMTOP = the byte below"},
        "413": {"comment":"CHARS = $3C00"},
        "419": {"comment":"The machine stack from RAMTOP down"},
        "430": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 4 set: 128 BASIC"},
        "435": {"comment":"$5B5F = $000B"},
        "451": {"comment":"$FF24 = $EC00"},
        "457": {"comment":"$5B64 = $50"},
        "462": {"comment":"$5B94 = $5B96 = 10"},
        "471": {"comment":"CHANS = $5CB6"},
        "477": {"comment":"The 21 bytes of CHANS_128_INIT"},
        "487": {"comment":"DATADD = the $80 at the end"},
        "491": {"comment":"PROG, VARS"},
        "498": {"comment":"The variables' end marker"},
        "501": {"comment":"E_LINE: an empty edit line"},
        "510": {"comment":"WORKSP, STKBOT, STKEND"},
        "519": {"comment":"ATTR_P, ATTR_T, BORDCR = $38"},
        "530": {"comment":"$EC13 = 0 (bank 7)"},
        "534": {"comment":"Border 7"},
        "538": {"comment":"REPDEL 35, REPPER 5"},
        "544": {"comment":"KSTATE: both sets free"},
        "550": {"comment":"STRMS from STRMS_INIT"},
        "565": {"comment":"ERR_NR = $FF"},
        "569": {"comment":"DF_SZ = 2"},
        "573": {"comment":"CLS (ROM 1)"},
        "576": {"comment":"ROM 1's test picture, with BREAK held"},
        "579": {"comment":"The copyright message"},
        "593": {"comment":"$5B81 = $5BFF: the other stack"},
        "599": {"comment":"Bank 7 and its stack"},
        "602": {"comment":"$EC11 = $EC0F = $38"},
        "610": {"comment":"EDITOR_RESET"},
        "613": {"comment":"Bank 0 and the machine stack"},
        "616": {"comment":"The main menu"},
        "1377": {"synopsis":"The start-up message, last character with bit 7 set: \"(c) 1986 Sinclair Research Ltd\" (the\nfirst byte is $7F, the copyright sign)."},
        "1405": {"synopsis":"Prints the text at DE through RST $10, up to and including the character with bit 7 set\n(printed without it). Changes: AF, DE."},
        "1407": {"comment":"Bit 7 off"},
        "1413": {"comment":"Bit 7 was set: done"},
        "1417": {"synopsis":"CHANS as start-up copies it to $5CB6: K (output $09F4, input $10A8), S ($09F4, $15C4), R\n($0F81, $15C4) as in the 48K ROM, then P with output $5B34 (CHAN_P_OUT) and input $5B2F\n(CHAN_P_IN), which reach ROM 0; $80 ends it."},
        "1438": {"synopsis":"STRMS as start-up copies it to $5C10: the offsets of streams -3 to 3 into CHANS."},
        "7268": {"synopsis":"Pages in the RAM bank BANK_NUMBERS gives for A (0-5: banks 1, 3, 4, 6, 7, 0) at $C000,\nkeeping the rest of the paging byte ($5B5C), with interrupts off. Keeps BC and HL."},
        "7277": {"comment":"C = the bank"},
        "7282": {"comment":"The old bank's bits cleared"},
        "7297": {"synopsis":"SELECT_BANK's banks for A = 0-5: 1, 3, 4, 6, 7, 0."},
        "7968": {"synopsis":"Back to RAM bank 0 (paging byte 0: ROM 0, normal screen) and to the stack kept in $5B81,\nwhich in turn keeps this one: the pair of BANK7_STACK. The return address goes with the\ncaller; AF and HL kept."},
        "7972": {"comment":"Paging byte 0"},
        "7975": {"comment":"The return address"},
        "7979": {"comment":"The stacks swapped"},
        "7994": {"synopsis":"Writes A to port $7FFD and to the paging byte at $5B5C. Keeps BC."},
        "8005": {"synopsis":"Swaps the stack with the one kept in $5B81, then pages RAM bank 7 in at $C000 (paging byte\n7): where the editor's own data lives ($EC00 up). The return address goes with the caller;\nAF and HL kept."},
        "8007": {"comment":"The return address"},
        "8011": {"comment":"The stacks swapped"},
        "8023": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "9527": {"synopsis":"A key table for TABLE_DISPATCH: a count ($15), then for each key its code and the address of\nits routine."},
        "9591": {"synopsis":"A key table for TABLE_DISPATCH: a count (4), then code and routine for each key."},
        "9604": {"synopsis":"Clears the editor's state: $28BE, $FC9A = 0, $EC0D = $82, E_PPC = 0, $35BC, $365E\n(KEY_DEFAULTS)."},
        "9631": {"synopsis":"The start-up menu: $5B81 = $5BFF, bank 7 and its stack (BANK7_STACK), stream 2; the menu's\nactions MENU_ACTIONS and text MAIN_MENU_TEXT into $F6EA and $F6EC; $EC0D bit 1 set, bit 4\nclear, $EC0C = 0; the menu drawn (DRAW_MENU), then the key loop (MAIN_KEY_LOOP)."},
        "9640": {"comment":"Stream 2: the screen"},
        "9645": {"comment":"The menu's actions"},
        "9651": {"comment":"Its text"},
        "9669": {"comment":"Drawn"},
        "9811": {"synopsis":"Waits for a key (WAIT_KEY), clicks (CLICK_A with PIP), and handles it (KEY_DISPATCH);\nforever, the stack reset to $5BFF each time."},
        "9814": {"comment":"The key mode"},
        "9817": {"comment":"A = the key"},
        "9821": {"comment":"The click"},
        "9828": {"comment":"Handled"},
        "9833": {"synopsis":"Handles key A: looked up in KEY_TABLE_B when $EC0D bit 1 is set (a menu is up), else in\nKEY_TABLE_A (TABLE_DISPATCH); a key found runs its routine (and a click when that returns no\ncarry). A key not found: with $EC0D bit 1 set, MODE = 0; otherwise, with $EC0D bit 0 set, a\nclick; below $A3, on at $28F1."},
        "9839": {"comment":"A menu up: its keys"},
        "9844": {"comment":"Otherwise the editor's"},
        "9847": {"comment":"Found: run"},
        "9857": {"synopsis":"Not in the table."},
        "9865": {"synopsis":"No menu up."},
        "9876": {"synopsis":"Below $A3: on at $28F1; otherwise ignored."},
        "9959": {"synopsis":"A click of PIP / 2 (CLICK_A)."},
        "9964": {"synopsis":"A short tone: DE = A, HL = $0C80, through ROM 1's TONE_OUT. Keeps IX."},
        "10052": {"synopsis":"The start-up menu's actions: a count (5), then for each item its number and routine: 0\n$2831, 1 $286C, 2 $2885, 3 $1B47, 4 $2816. MAIN_MENU_TEXT follows: a count (6), the title\n\"128\" padded with spaces and ended by $FF."},
        "10078": {"synopsis":"The start-up menu's items, last letter with bit 7 set: Tape Loader, 128 BASIC, Calculator,\n48 BASIC, Tape Tester, and a blank one."},
        "10128": {"synopsis":"The editor's menu: a count (5) and five item numbers and routines, then a count (6) and the\ntitle \"Options \" ended by $FF."},
        "10154": {"synopsis":"The editor's menu items: 128 BASIC, Renumber, Screen, Print, Exit, and a blank one."},
        "13918": {"synopsis":"MODE ($5C41) = 0, REPPER = 2, then KEY_MODE."},
        "13928": {"synopsis":"FLAGS bits 2 and 3 set; $5B66 bit 0 set when $EC0D bit 4 is set, else cleared."},
        "13951": {"synopsis":"Waits for a new key (FLAGS bit 5), takes it from LAST_K: codes $20 and up, and $06-$0F after\nROM 1's KI_CAPS_LOCK handling ($36A4) accepts them; $10-$1F are ignored. Exit: A = the key.\nKeeps HL."},
        "13955": {"comment":"A new key?"},
        "13969": {"comment":"$20 and up: a key"},
        "13973": {"comment":"$10-$1F: ignored"},
        "13977": {"comment":"Below $06: ignored"},
        "13988": {"synopsis":"ROM 1's KI_CAPS_LOCK ($10DB) on the key in A."},
        "13992": {"synopsis":"Draws the menu whose text is at HL (a count, a title ended by $FF, items ended by bit 7):\nthe area under it saved (MENU_AREA_SAVE), MENU_HEADER_TEXT and the title, the stripes\n(DRAW_STRIPES), MENU_GAP_TEXT, then each item at line 8 + n, column 7, padded with spaces to\n12 characters; a border drawn around it (PLOT_LINE), and the bar on the first item\n(MENU_BAR)."},
        "14105": {"synopsis":"Plots A pixels from H, L, stepping by BC each time (ROM 1's PLOT_SUB after its COORDS,\n$22E9)."},
        "14123": {"synopsis":"AT B, C through RST $10."},
        "14131": {"synopsis":"Prints the characters at HL through RST $10, up to the $FF that ends them."},
        "14139": {"synopsis":"Saves TV_FLAG, COORDS onwards (20 bytes) and the screen and attributes where the menu goes\nto $EEF6 on; MENU_AREA_BACK ($373E) puts them back."},
        "14142": {"synopsis":"The other way: back from $EEF6."},
        "14282": {"synopsis":"Moves the menu's bar to item A: the attribute row at $5907 + 32 x A, 14 cells."},
        "14316": {"synopsis":"DRAW_MENU's texts, each ended by $FF: the header's place and colours (AT 7,7; OVER 0;\nINVERSE 0; INK 7; PAPER 0; BRIGHT 1) from $37EC; PAPER 0, a space, PAPER 7, INK 0 from\n$37FA; at $3802 sixteen bytes of a diagonal stripe pattern; at $3812 the stripes' colours\n(INK 2, INK 6, INK 4, INK 5 over the pattern's characters)."},
        "14370": {"synopsis":"Draws the coloured stripes of a menu title: the pattern at $3802 copied to $5B98 and printed\n(the text at $3812) with CHARS pointed at it. Keeps BC, DE, HL."},
        "16334": {"synopsis":"Looks key A up in the table at HL (a count, then code and address per key) and runs the\nroutine found. Exit: no carry and NZ when not found; Z when found, carry as the routine\nreturned it."},
        "16336": {"comment":"B = the count"},
        "16338": {"comment":"This key?"},
        "16346": {"comment":"The next"},
        "16348": {"comment":"Not found: no carry"},
        "16353": {"synopsis":"Found: the routine run (TABLE_CALL), Z, its carry kept."},
        "16366": {"synopsis":"Jumps to HL."},
        "16367": {"synopsis":"Bytes nothing in this ROM's code reads: 'MB', 'SB', 'AC', 'RG' and 'KM', each after a 0,\nthen $01."}
      }
    }
  },
